        "title": "ARM and RISC-V: Modern RISC Designs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ARM64 (AArch64) dominates mobile and has taken a large slice of the server and desktop market via Apple Silicon and AWS Graviton. RISC-V is the open-source ISA that has become the standard for embedded systems and is growing toward datacenter use. Both are load-store RISC architectures with fixed 32-bit instruction encoding, but they made different design choices."
